+# Response to the CI/CD Security Review
+
+This documents the verification of an external security review of Nimbus
+(three "critical" findings + a list of high-value CI/CD observations), what was
+confirmed, what was corrected, and what was fixed.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Verdict summary
+
+| # | Review claim | Verdict | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **F1** | Signing oracle signs fully attacker-chosen terms (incl. `premiumAmount`), no auth, no account binding, no server-side pricing | **CONFIRMED** (with corrections — see §2) | `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` signed `body.premiumAmount`/`payoutAmount`/`threshold` as-received; `Quote` in `programs/nimbus/src/state.rs` has **no buyer field**; on-chain `buy_policy` (`lib.rs`) trusts the signed `premium_amount` and enforces only an LTV cap, not a price floor |
+| **F1b** | The sign route is 404/405 in production because `output: 'export'` strips API routes | **CONFIRMED** | `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` built `EXPORT_STATIC=true` (→ `next.config.js` `output: 'export'`), which drops route handlers; also it **swapped `merged-app` in** (which has no `/api` at all) |
+| **F1c** | Setting `QUOTE_SIGNER_SECRET_KEY` in CI build env → Next "inlines it into a static bundle" | **INCORRECT mechanism** (underlying risk real) — see §2.1 | Non-`NEXT_PUBLIC_` server vars are *not* inlined by Next; under `output: 'export'` the route is excluded from the build, not bundled |
+| **F2** | Security headers are inert: `_headers` does nothing on GitHub Pages; `test -f out/_headers` passes on a file with zero effect | **CONFIRMED** | `scripts/generate-security-headers.js` writes a `_headers` file (a Netlify/Cloudflare Pages convention GitHub Pages ignores); `security-gate.yml` checked `test -f out/_headers`; `next.config.js` `headers()` is also ignored under `output: 'export'` |
+| **F3** | Rate limiter trivially bypassable: `getClientIp` trusts `cf-connecting-ip`/`x-real-ip`/`x-forwarded-for`; in-memory `Map` resets on cold start | **CONFIRMED** (with corrections — see §2.3) | `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` `getClientIp`; `offchain/rate-limiter.ts` in-memory fallback; the `app/api/quotes/sign/middleware.ts` limiter is dead code (not a valid Next middleware location) |
+| **H1** | Write-all `GITHUB_TOKEN` defaults + unpinned remote code (`cargo install` each run, `trufflehog@main`, `peaceiris` with `contents: write`) | **CONFIRMED** | `ci.yml`/`sbom.yml`/`security-gate.yml` jobs had no `permissions:`; `deploy-pages.yml` had `contents: write`; `trufflesecurity/trufflehog@main` is a moving branch; `cargo install cargo-audit|geiger|license|sbom` unpinned |
+| **H2** | Known vulns deliberately shipped: `cargo audit --ignore …` + `security-gate.sh` allowlist | **CONFIRMED** | `ci.yml` had `--ignore RUSTSEC-2024-0344 --ignore RUSTSEC-2022-0093`; `programs/nimbus/.cargo/audit.toml` ignores RUSTSEC-2026-0204; `scripts/security-gate.sh` allowlists `next`/`lodash`/`glob`/`postcss`/`nanoid`/`serialize-javascript`/`shell-quote`/Solana stack |
+| **H3** | `docker-build` is a lie (no container, `|| true`); `solana-security` never exits non-zero | **CONFIRMED** | `ci.yml` "docker-build" only `test -f`'d files; `solana-security` used `cargo install … \|\| true`, `cargo geiger … \|\| echo`, and `WARNING` echoes with no `exit 1` |
+| **H4** | CodeQL + Security-Gate schedules both `disabled_inactivity` | **CONFIRMED** | `gh workflow list` showed both disabled; re-enabling from this sandbox returned `403` (owner must re-enable) |
+| **H5** | Deployed tree ≠ audited tree (merged-app swap; hardcoded devnet RPC) | **CONFIRMED** | `deploy-pages.yml` swapped `merged-app` → `app` and set `NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com` |
+| **H6** | No test job; `nonce = Date.now()`; 120s expiry; `QUOTE_SIGNER_ALLOW_PAST=true` | **CONFIRMED** (replay nuance — see §2.2) | `ci.yml` had no test job; sign route `nonce = BigInt(Date.now())`, `quoteExpiryUnix = now + 120`, `QUOTE_SIGNER_ALLOW_PAST` opt-in |
+
+**Bottom line:** the review is overwhelmingly accurate. Two of the three "critical"
+findings are correct as stated; the third (key inlining) has the right instinct but
+a wrong mechanism. A handful of minor details were corrected below.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Corrections to the review (for accuracy)
+
+### 2.1 Finding 1c — the secret is *not* "inlined into a static bundle"
+
+Next.js only inlines **`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`** variables into client bundles. A plain
+`QUOTE_SIGNER_SECRET_KEY` read inside a server route is **not** inlined, and under
+`output: 'export'` the route file is simply **excluded from the build** (which is
+exactly why the endpoint 404s in production).
+
+The *real* danger the reviewer is gesturing at is a naive "fix": if someone
+prefixes the secret `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or moves signing into a client component so the
+static site "works", the key **would** ship to the browser. The correct fix is
+neither — the signer must live in a server-side (or authenticated) service, and
+the secret must come from a runtime secret store, never a build-time env var.
+
+### 2.2 "Predictable nonce, no replay defense" — replay *is* defended on-chain
+
+`nonce = Date.now()` is predictable, but replay is separately blocked on-chain:
+`buy_policy` calls `validate_and_increment_nonce` (`nonce.rs`), which requires the
+per-buyer `QuoteNonce` nonce to be **strictly greater** than the last used, and
+stores `policy.quote_hash`. What is genuinely missing is **account binding** — the
+`Quote` struct has no buyer field, so a signed quote is a **bearer instrument** any
+buyer can redeem. That is the real gap worth fixing in Rust (see §4).
+
+### 2.3 The `middleware.ts` limiter is dead code
+
+`app/api/quotes/sign/middleware.ts` is not a valid Next.js middleware (middleware
+must live at the repo root). The **live** limiter is `PersistentRateLimiter`
+(`offchain/rate-limiter.ts`, Redis-backed with an in-memory fallback) invoked from
+the route. Both were keyed on the spoofable IP — now fixed in §3.
+
+### 2.4 Minor
+
+- There is **no repo-defined `postinstall`** script in `package.json`. The supply
+  chain concern is real but comes from unpinned `cargo install` + third-party
+  Actions, not a `postinstall` hook.
+- `cargo audit` advisories were **ignored twice** (CLI `--ignore` flags *and*
+  `.cargo/audit.toml`). The CLI flags are now removed (single source of truth).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Fixes applied in this session (code, tsc/lint-verified)
+
+All changes are on the working tree. Typecheck (`tsc --noEmit` app + offchain) and
+`next lint` are green.
+
+| Area | File(s) | Change |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Server-side pricing** | `lib/pricing.ts` (new), `app/api/quotes/calculate/route.ts`, `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` | Extracted the pricing model into one shared module. The sign route now **recomputes the fair premium from the payout**, rejects underpayment, caps payout at `MAX_PAYOUT_DOLLARS`, and signs the **server-authoritative** premium — a client can no longer request a near-zero premium for an arbitrary payout. Payout cap tightened from `$1e12` → `$1e6` (also fixes a `Number` safe-integer overflow at the old cap). |
+| **IP handling** | `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` | `getClientIp` only trusts proxy headers when the deployment signals a trusted proxy (`VERCEL=1` / `CLOUDFLARE=1`); otherwise it buckets to `direct` instead of trusting a forged header. |
+| **Nonce** | `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` | `nextNonce()` — monotonic `max(now, last+1)` instead of raw `Date.now()`. |
+| **Headers honesty** | `scripts/generate-security-headers.js` | Removed the false "GitHub Pages compatible" claim; documented that `_headers` is honored only by Netlify/Cloudflare Pages. |
+| **CI least-privilege + honesty** | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Added `permissions: contents: read`; removed duplicate `--ignore` flags (audit policy now lives only in `programs/nimbus/.cargo/audit.toml`); `solana-security` is now a **hard gate** (Rust has 0 `unsafe`/`panic!`/`.unwrap()`, so it passes); renamed the fake `docker-build` → `structure-and-license`; added a **`js-test`** job (`tsc` app + offchain, `next lint`). |
+| **Security gate** | `.github/workflows/security-gate.yml` | Added `permissions: contents: read` (gate + secrets-scan jobs); the `_headers` check now asserts real directives, not mere file existence; added SHA-pinning TODO (esp. `trufflehog@main`). |
+| **SBOM** | `.github/workflows/sbom.yml` | Added `permissions: contents: read`. |
+| **Pages deploy** | `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` | **Deleted** — the static Pages deploy (a) can't serve `/api` routes, (b) ignores `_headers`, and (c) deployed the untested `merged-app`. Deploy the real app to Vercel instead (see remediation guide §3). |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Remaining work (requires your machine / a new session)
+
+The session that pushed the PR is closed, and the sandbox token cannot touch
+`.github/workflows/` or re-enable disabled workflows. Do these from your account:
+
+1. **Push + PR this batch** from a new session (the changes above are uncommitted
+   on the working tree; `git diff` them, commit, push).
+2. **SHA-pin every Action** — `actions/checkout@v4`, `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`,
+   `returntocorp/semgrep-action@v1`, `github/codeql-action/*@v3`,
+   `gitleaks/gitleaks-action@v2`, and especially `trufflesecurity/trufflehog@main`.
+   Compute SHAs with `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/commits/<tag>` on your machine.
+   Pin `cargo install` tools to versions too (`cargo install cargo-audit --version <x>`).
+3. **Re-enable CodeQL + Security Gate** (Settings → Actions, or `gh workflow enable`
+   as *your* account), and make them **required checks** in branch protection.
+4. **Account binding (Rust)** — add a `buyer: Pubkey` field to `Quote`
+   (`programs/nimbus/src/state.rs`), verify it against `ctx.accounts.buyer` in
+   `buy_policy`, and update `lib/quote.ts` `serializeQuote` + the sign route to
+   include it. Requires `anchor build` + `anchor test` on your machine (toolchain
+   unavailable here). Until then, quotes remain bearer instruments.
+5. **Shrink the advisory surface** — swap `@solana/wallet-adapter-wallets` →
+   `@solana/wallet-adapter-phantom` (removes the `protobufjs`/Trezor/Stellar/
+   Particle chain), and plan the Next 14 → 15 upgrade. Both are detailed in
+   `docs/REMEDIATING_REMAINING_BLOCKERS.md` §4–§5. Then prune the matching entries
+   from `scripts/security-gate.sh` and `.cargo/audit.toml`.
+6. **Remove `merged-app/`** (archive it) now that `deploy-pages.yml` is gone.
+7. **`QUOTE_SIGNER_ALLOW_PAST=true`** — leave unset for any real deployment; it is
+   a demo affordance that lets the signer mint backdated quotes.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Severity framing (for the submission)
+
+Everything in Findings 1–3 is **real** but currently **non-exploitable in
+production**, because:
+
+- The signer endpoint is **not deployed** (static export drops it), and
+- The only deployment is **devnet with self-minted USDC** (no real funds).
+
+The moment Nimbus goes to a serverless host (Vercel) with the signer live, or to
+mainnet with real capital, Finding 1's economic hole (client-chosen premium bounded
+only by pool LTV) becomes the top risk — which is why the server-side pricing fix
+and the Rust account-binding change are the two highest-priority items above.
