+# Patches — `merged-app` archive & quote `buyer` binding
+
+This directory holds the ready-to-apply artifacts for the two follow-up changes
+to the security review (see `docs/SECURITY_REVIEW_RESPONSE.md`).
+
+---
+
+## 1. `0001-quote-buyer-binding.patch`
+
+Binds a signed quote to a specific buyer wallet, so a signed quote is no longer a
+**bearer instrument** that anyone who obtains it can redeem. This was the one
+remaining protocol-level gap in the review ("no account binding").
+
+### What it changes
+
+| File | Change |
+|---|---|
+| `programs/nimbus/src/state.rs` | Add `pub buyer: Pubkey` to the `Quote` struct (right after `policy_id`, so Borsh field order stays consistent) |
+| `programs/nimbus/src/lib.rs` | `buy_policy` now `require!`s `quote.buyer == ctx.accounts.buyer.key()` |
+| `lib/quote.ts` | `QuoteFields.buyer: Uint8Array` + 32-byte `buyer` serialized right after `policyId` (message length 83 → 115 bytes) |
+| `lib/nimbus.ts` | `SignedQuote.quote.buyer` (base58), IDL `Quote.buyer` field (`publicKey`), client message-integrity check, and the `buyPolicy` instruction arg |
+| `app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts` | Accepts + validates a required base58 `buyer` (32 bytes), includes it in the signed message and in the response |
+| `app/buy/page.tsx` | Sends `buyer: publicKey.toBase58()` in the sign request |
+| `scripts/demo-settle.ts` | Includes the admin pubkey as `buyer` in the demo quote |
+| `tests/security-audit.ts` | `fakeQuote` includes `buyer: attacker.publicKey` (keeps the anchor test's instruction layout valid) |
+
+> The buyer field is inserted at the **same position in all three serializations**
+> (Rust `try_to_vec`, `lib/quote.ts` `serializeQuote`, and the hand-written IDL in
+> `lib/nimbus.ts`), which is required for the on-chain Ed25519 verification to pass.
+> Serialization layout was verified: 115 bytes total, buyer at bytes 8..40.
+
+### How to apply
+
+```bash
+# from the repo root (a checkout that already has the deep-dive work, e.g. main
+# after the PR merge, or this working tree)
+git apply --check docs/patches/0001-quote-buyer-binding.patch   # dry run
+git apply docs/patches/0001-quote-buyer-binding.patch           # apply
+```
+
+The patch was round-trip verified in this session: applying it to a clean
+"before" tree reproduces the exact current files (all 8 files diff-clean).
+
+### How to verify after applying
+
+```bash
+npx tsc --noEmit                                # app typecheck
+npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.offchain.json      # offchain typecheck (demo-settle.ts)
+npm run lint                                    # eslint
+
+# On your machine with the Rust/Anchor toolchain (see
+# docs/REMEDIATING_REMAINING_BLOCKERS.md §1):
+anchor build
+anchor test        # tests/nimbus.ts + tests/security-audit.ts
+```
+
+> ⚠️ **Rust is not compiled in this sandbox** (toolchain unavailable). The two Rust
+> hunks are minimal (`+3` in `state.rs`, `+9` in `lib.rs`) and follow existing
+> patterns in the file (`nonce.rs` uses the same `x == *y.key()` deref form), but
+> you **must** run `anchor build` to confirm before deploying.
+
+---
+
+## 2. `merged-app` archive (staged, not a patch file)
+
+The duplicate static-export frontend was archived with `git mv` (rename
+preserved in history) and is **already staged** in the working tree:
+
+```bash
+git status --short
+#   R  merged-app/… -> docs/_archived-merged-app/…        (10 renames)
+#   M  tailwind.config.ts    (removed the merged-app content glob)
+#   M  tsconfig.json         (added docs/_archived-merged-app to exclude)
+```
+
+`tsconfig.json` and `tailwind.config.ts` were updated so the archived copy is no
+longer type-checked or scanned for Tailwind classes. To finish it, commit
+(staging is already done):
+
+```bash
+git commit -m "chore: archive the merged-app static-export duplicate
+
+The Pages deploy workflow was removed (see the security review response); the
+divergent merged-app/ frontend is now archived under docs/ so it is out of the
+build/typecheck path while its history is preserved."
+```
+
+Because this is a `git mv`, the rename survives a normal `git commit` of the
+staged index — no patch file is needed. (A `.patch` of the rename was considered
+and discarded: renames don't serialize well as plain text diffs.)
+
+---
+
+## Suggested commit for the buyer binding (new session)
+
+```bash
+git add programs/nimbus/src/state.rs programs/nimbus/src/lib.rs \
+        lib/quote.ts lib/nimbus.ts app/api/quotes/sign/route.ts \
+        app/buy/page.tsx scripts/demo-settle.ts tests/security-audit.ts
+git commit -m "feat(program): bind signed quotes to the buyer wallet
+
+Add a buyer Pubkey to the on-chain Quote and enforce quote.buyer == signer in
+buy_policy, so a signed quote is no longer a bearer instrument. Mirrors the
+field in lib/quote.ts, the hand-written IDL, the sign API, the buy UI, and the
+demo script (Borsh layout verified: 115 bytes, buyer at bytes 8..40)."
+```
+
+Then push and open a new PR from the new session.
